# Collections and aggregates: Jo Nesbø's two short story collections
#
#   Sjalusimannen og andre fortellinger (Aschehoug, 2021), 7 stories
#   Rotteøya og andre fortellinger (Aschehoug, 2021), 5 stories
#
# Modelled as works and expressions at two levels: each story is a work of its
# own (genre entedit:T02, individual short stories), and each collection is a
# work (entedit:T01, short story collections) that has the stories as parts.
# The aggregates that bring both collections together are a third level:
#
#   - Aschehoug's 2022 paperback holds all 12 stories, but under the title of
#     the first collection only, "Sjalusimannen og andre fortellinger".
#   - The English translation by Robert Ferguson, "The jealousy man and other
#     stories" (Harvill Secker and Knopf, 2021), holds all 12 in two parts,
#     "Jealousy" and "Power".
#   Both are expressions of one omnibus work (entedit:T04) whose parts are the
#   two collection works.
#
# The French translations (Céline Romand-Monnier, Gallimard, Série noire) came
# out as two books, "De la jalousie" (2022) and "Rat Island" (2024). Only the
# collection level is recorded for them: the French titles of the individual
# stories are left out, as an exercise.
#
# A manifestation embodies the expression of the collection (or omnibus) and
# the expressions of every story it contains. The order of the stories is not
# recorded (it needs RDF-star, entedit:valueOrder), so lists fall back to title
# order.
#
# Sources: Nasjonalbiblioteket (api.nb.no) for the Norwegian editions, BnF for
# the French, library catalogues and the publishers for the English.
# Identifiers are ad hoc (http://example.org/nesbo/...).

@prefix entedit: <http://oslomet.no/abi/vocab#> .
@prefix rdaad: <http://rdaregistry.info/Elements/a/datatype/> .
@prefix rdac: <http://rdaregistry.info/Elements/c/> .
